  </div>

  <h2 id="tcpip-model" class={sectionH2}>
    <Icon name="globe" size={20} class={css({ color: 'primary' })} /> The TCP/IP 4-layer model
  </h2>
  <p class={bodyP}>
    The Internet Protocol Suite — what's actually running underneath every connection — predates OSI and
    collapses the top three OSI layers into one, since real applications never cleanly separate session,
    presentation, and application concerns the way OSI's telling does.
  </p>

  <div class={stack} data-layer-stack>
    {
      TCPIP_LAYERS.map((l, i) => (
        <div class={layerRow}>
          <span class={spineDot} aria-hidden="true" style={{ filter: `hue-rotate(${TCPIP_HUES[i]}deg)` }} />
